WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.100
- If you're currently using Basecamp 2

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.660
and considering upgrading to
Basecamp 5, the process

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.020
of moving is easier than you might think.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.680
This video, I'm going to
walk you through exactly how

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.620
to do it so you can see it for yourself.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.080
The first thing you'll
need to do is sign up

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.960
for a new Basecamp 5
account on basecamp.com.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.000
Make sure you use the same email address

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.040
that you're using in Basecamp 2.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.540
That way you can easily switch

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.560
between the two accounts without having

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.760
to log out and log back in.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.080
From your new Basecamp 5
account, head to Adminland

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.381
and click move projects from
Basecamp 2 to Basecamp 5.

00:00:34.381 --> 00:00:36.381
You'll want to read over the overview

00:00:36.381 --> 00:00:38.601
explaining how it all works.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.001
You'll then see a list

00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:43.821
of all your Basecamp 2
projects that are ready to move.

00:00:43.821 --> 00:00:45.821
Click the move over button to the right

00:00:45.821 --> 00:00:48.401
of any project you'd like to migrate.

00:00:48.401 --> 00:00:50.741
The time it'll take to move can vary

00:00:50.741 --> 00:00:52.101
as it depends on the size

00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:54.741
of the projects you're moving over.

00:00:54.741 --> 00:00:56.521
As soon as the projects are moved over,

00:00:56.521 --> 00:00:58.861
you'll get a notification by email.

00:00:58.861 --> 00:01:02.781
You'll then see those projects
archived in Basecamp 2

00:01:02.781 --> 00:01:05.362
and active in Basecamp 5.

00:01:05.362 --> 00:01:08.702
Now, how clients are handled
in Basecamp 2 is quite a bit

00:01:08.702 --> 00:01:11.362
different for how they're
handled in Basecamp 5

00:01:11.362 --> 00:01:14.302
So if you happen to have
a list of client projects

00:01:14.302 --> 00:01:17.102
that aren't able to
move over, not to worry,

00:01:17.102 --> 00:01:19.722
those projects can't move automatically,

00:01:19.722 --> 00:01:23.382
but turning the project's
client feature off in Basecamp

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.282
2 will fix that.

00:01:25.282 --> 00:01:28.062
Just access the client
project you'd like to move,

00:01:28.062 --> 00:01:32.162
select invite more people,
then click the client tab.

00:01:32.162 --> 00:01:36.022
From here, you'll remove any
clients listed on this page.

00:01:36.022 --> 00:01:39.083
When that's finished,
select "Turn this option off."

00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:42.083
You'll now have no trouble
moving the project into Basecamp

00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.303
5 and you can invite your clients back

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.083
to the project from there.

00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:49.603
So now that you've moved your
projects over to Basecamp 5,

00:01:49.603 --> 00:01:52.583
what do you do with your
Basecamp 2 account?

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:55.043
Well, if you're planning
to use Basecamp 5

00:01:55.043 --> 00:01:56.843
for all your new projects,

00:01:56.843 --> 00:02:00.703
your Basecamp 2 account
will qualify for a free plan.

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:03.863
You'll be able to finish out
any existing projects you've

00:02:03.863 --> 00:02:05.923
already started in Basecamp two

00:02:05.923 --> 00:02:09.544
and you can easily access
your archived projects forever.

00:02:09.544 --> 00:02:11.244
You just won't be able to create new

00:02:11.244 --> 00:02:12.664
projects in Basecamp 2.

00:02:13.704 --> 00:02:16.624
After adding your credit card
to your Basecamp 5 account,

00:02:16.624 --> 00:02:19.944
you can switch your Basecamp
2 account to a free plan.

00:02:19.944 --> 00:02:21.604
Just go to your account page

00:02:21.604 --> 00:02:24.864
and click the switch
to this package button

00:02:24.864 --> 00:02:27.124
under billing and invoices.

00:02:27.124 --> 00:02:29.524
If you plan to create new
projects in both versions

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:31.104
of Basecamp, that's fine too.

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:33.744
Just keep in mind you'll
have to pay for Basecamp 2

00:02:33.744 --> 00:02:36.764
and Basecamp 5
separately when you do that.

00:02:36.764 --> 00:02:39.704
Most people who make the
transition don't continue making

00:02:39.704 --> 00:02:43.045
new projects in the earlier
version, but you have options.

00:02:43.045 --> 00:02:44.785
If you have any questions about making the

00:02:44.785 --> 00:02:46.345
switch, reach out to our support team.

00:02:46.345 --> 00:02:49.645
They're available by email
at support@basecamp.com.

